  "scope": "The source configs/raw bytes are preserved, and only original ordinary levels1\u2013100 are imported byte-for-byte. A lightweight ScriptableObject stores weak resource paths; actual runtime loads only the selected payload. The formal first-board entry now uses this catalog, and account/area startup plus its identity/test transport are removed per the new scope. Native session reset still receives mandatory inventory snapshots, now authored session presentation values rather than a persistent account. SDK mock handling is unchanged. Unity sequentially loads100 configurations and verifies real first-board presentation/input; this does not make unsupported later obstacle/static compositions playable. The first-board composition guard, required first100 obstacle/goal models, complete production win/fail/remaining-moves/end/retry/next-level/local-progress flow and remaining booster inventory/purchase UI removal remain pending. No higher-level/peripheral implementation, whole filesystem rollback, full rendered parity or mobile completion is claimed."
}
